## 7. Verification & Test Harness (How The Test Works: 1-SSOT Tri-Corpus)

This rule is rigorously tested and validated across the canonical **1-SSOT Tri-Corpus** in `tests/correctness/{{ .ID }}/`:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph GoldenCorpus ["1-SSOT Tri-Corpus Test Matrix for {{ .ID }}"]
        subgraph P ["Positive Corpus (tests/correctness/{{ .ID }}/positive/)"]
            P1["P1: Obvious Direct Violation"]
            P2["P2: Indirect / Variant Concatenation"]
            P3["P3: Helper / clsx / cn Wrapper"]
            P4["P4: Deeply Nested Elements"]
            P5["P5: Aliased Imports / Re-exports"]
        end
        subgraph N ["Negative Corpus (tests/correctness/{{ .ID }}/negative/)"]
            N1["N1: Valid Design Tokens"]
            N2["N2: Explicit charites:ignore Directive"]
            N3["N3: Third-Party / Vendor Components"]
            N4["N4: Clean Semantic HTML"]
            N5["N5: Untokenized Custom Values (Banana Test)"]
        end
        subgraph A ["Adversarial Corpus (tests/correctness/{{ .ID }}/adversarial/)"]
            A1["A1: Template Literal Interpolations"]
            A2["A2: Ternary Conditional Expressions"]
            A3["A3: Spread Properties & Dynamic Overrides"]
            A4["A4: Dynamic Object Class Syntax"]
            A5["A5: Shadowed Variable Identifiers"]
            A6["A6: Nested Closures & HOC Wrappers"]
            A7["A7: Obfuscated Classes & Cyclic Tokens"]
        end
    end

    P --> TestRunner["Automated Runner (rule_test.go)"]
    N --> TestRunner
    A --> TestRunner
    TestRunner --> Gates["Quality Gates: Zero Panic, Zero False-Positive, Zero Bypass"]
```

- **Positive Fixtures (P1-P5):** Verified to trigger diagnostics at exact lines and column spans.
- **Negative Fixtures (N1-N5):** Verified to produce zero diagnostics on valid tokens and legitimate exemptions.
- **Adversarial Fixtures (A1-A7):** Verified to prevent evasion across dynamic expressions, string interpolations, and cyclic references.

